{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1397696-homebrew-setting-the-lowlands-of-the-world-of-darkness","id":1397696,"title":"HomeBrew Setting: The Lowlands of The World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-20T05:54:05-07:00","id":1397696,"title":"HomeBrew Setting: The Lowlands of The World of Darkness","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here, for the pleasure of your critical eyes, I present the humble first drafts of my attempt at the furtive brewing of homegrown content for the exalted game of Mage: The Awakening.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is just an unfinished product I've tinkered with and abandoned many time over the pas year, I'll give you two excerpts here and post a link to the Google doc for the fullness of what I've yet to finish.</span></span></span></div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Land Under-sea-and-wind, The Wetlands, The Wooded Sands, The Boughten Land, The Lands Downriver, The Forgotten Kingdom in the Middle\u2026</i></span></span></b></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These are but a few of the cognomen and kennings by which the Lowlands are known in the hidden World of Darkness. The continental corner of europe that most people nowadays think of as the Kingdom of the Netherlands has been known by many names over the ages. Few of those names ever paid much heed to the imaginary lines rulers like to draw in their heads. Nevertheless, over the years much of the identity and cultural heritage of these sodden lands has been co-opted by one or two political entities. Thanks in no small part to the rise of Nation-States and \u201cNational Identities\u201d over the last few centuries, when one speaks of the Low Countries/Lands people generally assume you\u2019re speaking of either just the Netherlands or with the inclusion of the Flemish state of the Kingdom of Belgium. These regions are mostly unified in their high representation of Dutch-speaking peoples. Within the context of recorded history alone this a very recent distinction, which has neglected a larger cultural heritage that has been ingrained in the wider region since long before the romans decided to write down how the \u201csavages\u201d lived up there in Germania. Thanks to the vagaries of empire, religion, and convenience various parts of modern day Belgium, The Netherlands, Germany, France and Luxembourg have all been billeted together at some point or another. The peoples, customs, and languages of these regions have intermingled, drifted, disappeared, and been added to, countless times. Yet certain commonalities remain regardless of official boundaries, appellations, or designations...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The latter question caused the most contention between the nameless orders and during the peak of the Dutch Golden Age a small cabal of nameless mages, inheritors of the inter-city mage alliances, focused on the potential of trade and commerce, rose to prominence. This cabal had involved itself with the interests of various merchant endeavours for decades and had nourished the founding of multiple trading companies culminating in the unprecedented success of the VOC, the dutch east-india trading company. The cabal promoted the concept of Enlightened self-interest and advocated direct but subtle meddling in sleeper economics. Their philosophy held that through the creation of wealth from products with seemingly little practical value or even from things that existed solely within the mind, sleepers where performing a kind of awakened magic themselves, a kind of Supernal alchemy. This philosophy naturally attracted many Alchemist Moros and other spiritually and necromantically inclined mages. The cabal quickly grew into a full fledged Nameless Order and started to spread their influence throughout the region in ways the Diamond had not for centuries. Many of the other Nameless Cabals, Legacies, and Orders were incorporated into the Company, the rest were too inconsequential to incorporate or held strong against the rising tide of the newly named \u201cVerhevene Verenichde Vere Horizone Compagnie\u201d, in later times shortened to the Far Horizons Company (Vere Horizons Compagnie) or VHC/FHC. While the Company rode the tides of international commerce better than many others did, it stopped short of complete dominance and settled into an argumentative peace with the rest of the Awakened in the region....&quot;</span></span></span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;...</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another curiosity to be found on the bussy and historical Damrak is a massive Aedes of Stygian nature. 'Het Huis van de Pauper Aandeelhouder' or 'The House of the Pauper Shareholder' as it's known in English, is one of the oldest recurring mysteries of the city. The House of the Shareholder, or The House of the Pauper for the slightly more cynical, seems to appear sporadically in the Stygian reflection of the Damrak, adhering to a schedule that few if any have ever deciphered. Nor is it entirely exclusive to the Dutch capital. It has appeared a handful times in distant places across the world. These notable exceptions might hold the key to figuring out it's timetable. The Shells that tell the tale of the Pauper Shareholder symbolise an Archetypical manifestation of the classic \u201crags to riches\u201d story. Yet the supernal is a duplicitous mistress and smashes pigeon holes upon the walls of infinite complexity. The House of the Shareholder is the supernal home of the eponymous great being of deceptively modest bearing. The Pauper is a figure of duality, of seeming contradiction that encompasses the whole. Across history many an alchemist seeking out this mystery came to parse the Aedes through various occult lenses, yet always came back to this duality. The Sun and Moon, Yin and Yang, God and Satan, the symbologies with which these Moros described their Supernal visions where of little help to their awakened colleagues when it came to unravelling the Mysteries of this figure and it's exalted domain. This all changed when a fairly young, yet deceptively powerful woman came to the city, lured by an ancient call. This young Obrimos had awakened under a series of unusual circumstances in colonial Ciudad de Mexico. The mestizo girl had already lived through more adventures by the age of 25 than many an exalted magister of the diamond had when she came to the Merchant Country, on the cusp of unleashing a revolutionarily old, new legacy upon the world. A short raven haired girl walked up to the middle of the Damrak one morning in the summer of 1765 and addressed the empty air as the Lord and Lady of Humble Beginnings, summoning the full force of the Aedes into existence. The small figure, </span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>extremely</i></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">small to the locals, bowed before the manifestation of the Pauper Shareholder and offered them the sun and moon in the palms of her hands, which seemed to amuse the Supernal being. The fact that the girl reportedly spoke in her ancestral Nahuatl dialect makes this popular version of the tale somewhat suspect. But it was on that day that the Theme of the Aedes became plain to see to all who would look upon it, as it already had been to the girl, more than a century after its first appearance. The Creation of the Valuable, the Worthy, out of That Which is Not....&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Full thing in the works here:<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11c4rAgucnHDrjInZNf1RidHujJ4zEumVVstzvNs_cHk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I've mostly not done anything mechanics-wise yet, but that's also being worked on like a couple legacies, mechanics for the aedes above and other things.<br /> <br /> Let me know this seems interesting to anybody, peace.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26103-alambril","user":"Alambril","date":". 06-20-2020, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26103-alambril","name":"Alambril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}